/docs/core

core, or, core:: namespace, is a compiler provided interface to change compiler behavior, get constants, edit parameters,
and interact with compiler overall, core contains different things, like compiler defined variables, global data, and so on,
only some parameters will have the permission of being overwritten, every file gets its own private copy so you can implement your
own core behavior, but now in lstc.

core::asm

.syscall(args) -
Syscall using params, first param is the syscall number.
core::asm! {
    /-/ platform independent asm
    add(2foo, *bar);
    mov(sys(0), 60);
    mov(sys(1), 0);
    syscall(); /-/ asm blocks are never optimized by the compiler
    /-/ but, it can be "transformed" to match functionality.
}
